gaps.proposedFix:
{ "repeatUntil": "state.depth == 0", "max": 4096, "as": "propertyValue",
  "fields": [ { "ref": "messages.bacnetTag" } ] }
plus a decode-writable accumulator field:
{ "set": "state.depth", "value": "state.depth + 1", "when": "capture.lvt == 6" }
{ "set": "state.depth", "value": "state.depth - 1", "when": "capture.lvt == 7" }
`max` mirrors §4's `loop.max` rule so the packet/work bound stays computable. This one primitive also retires the CoAP option-delta and DNS-compression gaps in §5.

State the rule in §3 and make it explicit at the field:
{ "u16be": "len(group:bvll)", "selfInclusive": true }
Rule text: a span expression referring to a group that contains the referring field is LEGAL and not cyclic, provided every field between them has a statically known width; it is a validation error only if a width in the span itself depends on the field being patched. Also add `len(message)` for 'everything on the wire'.

Add to the numeric converter group: `bit(n)`, `bits(hi,lo)`, `shl(n)`, `shr(n)`, `and(m)`, `or(m)`, `mod(m)`.
{ "value":"capture.objectIdentifier | shr(22)", "as":"objectType" }
{ "u16be":null, "as":"dnet", "when":"capture.npduControl | bit(5) == 1" }
Smallest fix that generalises — six converters retire the majority of the `when`-on-decode pain without any engine change.

"messages": {
  "ctxTag": { "params":["num","lvt"],
              "fields":[ {"bits":[ {"n":4,"value":"params.num"},
                                   {"n":1,"value":"1"},
                                   {"n":3,"value":"params.lvt"} ]} ] } }
…
{ "ref":"messages.ctxTag", "with": { "num":0, "lvt":4 } }
Permit self-reference with a declared bound — { "ref":"messages.bacnetTag", "maxDepth":16 } — mirroring §4's rule that back edges must carry loop.max, so the work bound stays computable.

"effects": {
  "negotiate": {
    "txn.windowSize": "min(capture.proposedWindowSize, inputs.maxWindow)",
    "store.dev.segmentationSupported": "capture.abortReason != 4",
    "store.dev.maxApduGranted": "min(capture.maxApduCode, inputs.maxApduCode)" },
  "confidence": "confirmed" }
and let `requires` read the negotiated result, not just prior message names:
"requires": [ "store.dev.segmentationSupported == true" ]

"states": {
  "commsDisabled": {
    "exclusive": true,
    "allows": ["deviceCommunicationControl","reinitializeDevice"],
    "expires": "store.dccExpiresUtc",
    "failureMode": "silent",
    "ambiguousWith": ["offline","packetLoss"],
    "disambiguateBy": { "probe":"messages.whoIs", "afterMs":3000 } } }
`exclusive: true` makes any message not in `allows` a validation error while in this state; `failureMode: "silent"` tells the engine that a timeout here is evidence, not just an error.

Add a per-field re-encode policy so captured bytes win over recomputation:
{ "u16be":"len(group:bvll)", "as":"bvlcLength", "onReencode":"preserveCaptured" }
{ "bits":[ {"n":1,"as":"reserved","onReencode":"preserveCaptured"}, … ] }
and a document-level switch "roundTrip": "byteExact | canonical" so a test harness can demand exactness while normal operation still derives. For the length-form ambiguity, have the extended-`tlv` fix capture the FORM alongside the value: "as":{"length":"len","lengthForm":"lenForm"}.
